    "true": "A transparent open U-shaped tube holds a dense liquid in both arms and the connecting bend, with a lighter immiscible oil column above the dense liquid in the left arm. The two free surfaces start at different heights while the bottom valve is closed. An actuator opens the valve and withdraws. Both liquid levels move and settle with the oil-side free surface visibly higher than the other free surface, as the two actual densities determine the pressure balance."
